The parts of `fs::basic_path` that do not depend on the allocator, compiled once in the
library instead of once per allocator type.

- `path_text.hpp`: normalization (`path_append_components`, which collapses slashes and drops "."
  components while copying), name checks, glob matching (`*`, `?`, `[abc]`, `[a-z]`, `[!x]`) and
  the lexical `match` and `relative_to` on already-normalized text, plus the system queries
  behind `exists` and the kind tests, for which a missing path or a non-directory parent
  (`path_is_missing`) means false rather than an error.
- `read_to_end.hpp`: reads a whole descriptor into a `dynamic_array`, sized from `fstat` first and
  grown when the file is longer than it said (as files in /proc are): what `read_text` and
  `read_bytes` use.
